=== day
n: 5
title: Functions and decisions
subtitle: Reusable code, if and else
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: @page, page.js

--- intro
Yesterday you wrote instructions that run once, from top to bottom. Today you package them into **functions**: named pieces of code you can run again and again, with different numbers each time.

The page shows four show cards. Every card has grey notes like *(write watchTime)*. A helper file, **page.js**, is already written: it runs after your code and uses your functions to fill in the cards. So each function you finish makes all four cards light up at once.

You'll also learn the most important difference in today's lesson: a function can *print* a value, or *give it back*. Only one of them fills the cards.

